{:edb/db-before-t 1479 :edb/db-after-t 1480 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534792 50 #inst "2026-10-08T07:00:55.194Z" 13194139534792 true] [17592186129054 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310447 13194139534792 true] [17592186129189 1020 #edb/ref 17592186310454 13194139534792 true] [17592186129433 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534792 true] [17592186129433 1145 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume $V$ of a balloon** being inflated **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the volume**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of volume.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310447 1017 #edb/ref 17592186310448 13194139534792 true] [17592186310447 1089 "q-119054" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310447 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534792 true] [17592186310447 1100 "The amount of money $M(t)$ in a saving account increases at a rate that is proportional to the amount of money currently in the account. What differential equation describes the rate of change in the amount of money in the saving account $M,$ at time $t?$" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310447 1113 #uuid "fa32ad2d-05af-5067-9118-2c0c283b8d2a" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310447 1145 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **amount of money** $M(t)$ in a saving account **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **amount of money** currently in the saving account.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *amount of money* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *amount of money.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}∝M.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the amount of money *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kM.\n$$" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310449 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310450 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310451 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310452 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1000 #edb/ref 17592186310453 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1041 "selection" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1104 #edb/ref 17592186310451 13194139534792 true] [17592186310448 1110 #uuid "c61bbc42-877d-5f75-b824-673922e2d663" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310449 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}\\text{M}}{\\text{d}t}=-kM,\\,k>0" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310449 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534792 true] [17592186310449 1111 #uuid "5d7149ac-2bbd-5157-b847-7e20a49ac8d3" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310450 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}\\text{M}}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{M},\\,k>0" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310450 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534792 true] [17592186310450 1111 #uuid "a240a70d-4182-51c1-9562-8bd784e6db5d" 13194139534792 true] [17592186310451 103